<template><ResearchShell dark><main class="launch-page launch-prose">
 <p class="launch-eyebrow">{{ previewMode?'Project preview':'Your research workspace' }}</p><h1>{{ title }}</h1>
 <template v-if="page==='privacy'"><p v-if="previewMode">This preview uses illustrative examples. It does not submit uploaded files, stock tickers, passwords or payment details. Your chosen example team is stored in your browser. GitHub Pages may keep standard hosting access logs.</p><template v-else><p>Your account and saved research are private. The service uses your email and authentication details to manage access; submitted charts, research context and generated reports are used to provide your analyses.</p><p>The hosted service uses Supabase for accounts and database records, private Cloudflare R2 storage for files, a server for processing, and the configured model API to analyse the information you submit. Stripe handles subscription payments and Brevo delivers account emails.</p><p>You can delete reports or request account deletion in your account. Account deletion stops analyses and removes research files and account data. Minimal billing and usage records are retained where needed for accounting, dispute resolution and abuse prevention.</p></template></template>
 <template v-else-if="page==='terms'"><p v-if="previewMode">This project preview demonstrates the interface with fictional or explicitly labelled sample information. No subscriptions, account services or live analyses are provided here.</p><template v-else><p>Stock Lab and Chart Lab provide research, conditional scenarios and simulated agent perspectives. Outcomes are uncertain. Outputs can contain errors and do not guarantee returns or execute trades.</p><p>Plans provide the displayed daily analysis allowance shared across both labs. Allowances reset at midnight UTC and do not roll over. Saved reports remain available after a subscription ends unless you delete them.</p><p>Paid subscriptions renew monthly. Upgrades require payment confirmation. Scheduled downgrades and cancellations take effect at the end of the paid period. Technical failures without a useful result restore the analysis allowance; this is separate from a payment refund.</p><p>Submit only material you have the right to use. Do not attempt to bypass account limits, access another user's data or interfere with the service.</p></template></template>
 <template v-else><p v-if="previewMode">Live accounts, uploads and payments will be available in the hosted application. Use the example team selector to explore all three tiers in this preview.</p><p v-else>For billing, use Manage billing in your account. If an analysis is interrupted, its saved work remains available for recovery.</p><p v-if="email">Contact <a :href="'mailto:'+email">{{ email }}</a>.</p><p v-else>Support contact details will be published before the hosted service opens.</p></template>
 <p v-if="!previewMode&&!account.config?.analyses_enabled" class="launch-notice">Pre-launch information. Operator details, data permissions and these policies require review before paid public access opens.</p>
 <footer class="launch-footer"><RouterLink to="/">Research home</RouterLink><RouterLink to="/pricing">Plans</RouterLink><RouterLink to="/privacy">Privacy</RouterLink><RouterLink to="/terms">Terms</RouterLink></footer>
 </main></ResearchShell></template>
<script setup>
import {computed} from 'vue'
import {useRoute} from 'vue-router'
import ResearchShell from '../components/ResearchShell.vue'
import {account,previewMode} from '../api/platform'
import '../styles/launch.css'
const route=useRoute(),page=computed(()=>route.path.slice(1)),title=computed(()=>({privacy:'Your privacy.',terms:'Terms of use.',support:'How can we help?'}[page.value]||'About this workspace.'))
const email=computed(()=>/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(account.config?.support_email||'')?account.config.support_email:'')
</script>
